.TH "DOT\-LN" "1" "August 2026" ""
.SH "NAME"
\fBdot\-ln\fR \- Link managed dotfiles from repo to home directory
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBdot ln\fR [\-h] [\fIfile\fR\|\.\|\.\|\.]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Link one or more managed dotfiles from the dotfile repository\.
.IP "\(bu" 4
If a file is not linked, it will link it\.
.IP "\(bu" 4
If a file is already linked correctly, it will exit\.
.IP "\(bu" 4
If a file is linked incorrectly, it will throw an error informing you to remove it with dot\-rm(1) first and exit\.
.IP "" 0
.P
Part of dot(1)\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-h\fR
Show command help\.
.TP
[\fIfile\fR]
One or more managed files (optional)\. Paths are relative to the dotfile repo\. If no files are passed, all managed files will be linked\.

